{"ts":1781473518026,"state_hash":"0e344b328bb667f2","passage":"Canvas_aud_teachme_Node_1","engine":"sugarcube","body_text":"Canvas: Teach me (aud_teachme) | Node: Teach me\n\n\n\n[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/aud_teachme.jpg\n\nIt takes her a few days to circle back, and when she does it isn't about money. She's been working herself up to it — you can see the rehearsal in how she won't quite look at you, picking at the hem of her sleeve while the textbook on her knees goes unread. There's a boy, she finally says. Danny. He's in her seminar and he's kind and he doesn't see her at all, not the way she wants, and she doesn't know how to make him.\n\nYou always know how to make people — I don't know — want you. Want to do things for you. I've watched you do it my whole life. Could you just… teach me how? How to be like that. For him.\n\nYou let the question sit while you look at her properly — the softness of her, the trust of her, the wide-open way she's handing you the exact lever you'd have spent weeks building yourself. She thinks she's asking for Danny. You tell her yes. Of course. You'll teach her everything you know about being wanted, and the two of you will start whenever she's ready — and you let her think the whole time that the lessons are about a boy who isn't in the room.\n\n💭 Audrey is thinking: She said yes. God, if anyone can fix this it's her. I'm going to do whatever she says and Danny is finally going to look at me.\n💭 You are thinking: She brought me the leash and asked me to put it on her. I'll teach her to want, all right. Just not for him.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTell her you'll teach her.","body_html":"<div class=\"dev-canvas-info\"><strong>Canvas:</strong> Teach me <span style=\"opacity:0.7;\">(aud_teachme)</span> | <strong>Node:</strong> Teach me</div><br><div style=\"border:2px dashed #666;padding:20px;margin:10px 0;border-radius:8px;background:#f5f5f5;\"><p style=\"margin:0;font-weight:bold;color:#333;\">[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/aud_teachme.jpg</p></div